<title>FRANCE: Algeria tells freed Islamist leader &quot;no politics&quot;.</title>
<headline>Algeria tells freed Islamist leader &quot;no politics&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria on Friday ordered newly freed Islamic Salvation Front (FIS) leader Abassi Madani to refrain from political activity, the interior ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Madani, who was freed on parole from prison last Tuesday, halfway through a 12-year sentence imposed in 1992, has since been meeting former aides and making statements to journalists.</p>
